@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: why the in-container prep is a Go subprocess and what it therefore cannot hand the agent
' covers: cmd/proveo-entrypoint/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/entrypoint/**
' covers: internal/contract/contract_test.go (TestEntrypointsRunTheShellPreludeThenPrep)
' covers: internal/contract/env_prelude_test.go (TestPrepKeepsOnlyWhatCrossesTheBoundary)
'
' ── N1 (DONE (wt) 2026-10-17): prep KEEPS ONLY WHAT CROSSES THE BOUNDARY ───
' Part of the user's "apply fixes for SEC2, SEC3, N1, F18, …" (repo-simplification.puml
' N1, option 1). MEASURED: `proveo-entrypoint prep [target]` runs EnsureRuntimeUser
' (the passwd entry), the git-context report and the smoke sentinel, nothing else
' (cmd/proveo-entrypoint/main.go:52-64); internal/entrypoint holds only
' EnsureRuntimeUser, SmokeReady and firstNonEmpty. The exec mode
' (`proveo-entrypoint <target> -- cmd`) is deleted; usage is
' `prep [target] | verify [dir] | adb-mirror`. BridgeGoogleKeys, BridgeGitIdentity,
' NormalizeModel and ApplyEnvBridges are deleted with their tests, and so is the
' chdir. Every process-local step is the SHELL's now: each def entrypoint runs
' set_working_directory, bridge_google_keys and bridge_git_identity, then
' `proveo-entrypoint prep` (e.g. defs/codex/entrypoint.sh:12-16); the `else`
' branches for an image without the binary are gone.
' FLAGGED (image agent; consequences to confirm, recorded not decided here):
'   * the ORDER is reversed — the shell prelude runs BEFORE prep, so prep's git
'     report sees the working directory and identity the shell set;
'   * agents now RECEIVE the git-identity env — bridge_git_identity exports in
'     the shell the agent inherits, where its Go twin exported into a dying child.
' Pinned by TestEntrypointsRunTheShellPreludeThenPrep and
' TestPrepKeepsOnlyWhatCrossesTheBoundary. [Unverified] in a built image: the image
' suites did not run this pass (1.9 GB of disk free, reported).
title proveo-entrypoint prep — only what crosses the process boundary

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {

  component "defs/<name>/entrypoint.sh\n(PID 1 shell — execs the agent)" as SH <<app>>

  frame "In-shell prelude (FIRST)\nentrypoint-lib.sh" as SHELLPRE {
    component "set_working_directory\nchdir(2)" as CWD <<app>>
    component "bridge_google_keys\nGoogle key alias exports" as ENV <<app>>
    component "bridge_git_identity\nGIT_CONFIG_KEY_n exports" as GITID <<app>>
  }

  component "proveo-entrypoint prep <target>\n(child process, AFTER the prelude)" as PREP <<app>>

  frame "Crosses the boundary\n(external to the process)" as OK {
    component "EnsureRuntimeUser\npasswd entry + writable HOME" as UID <<app>>
    component "git-context report\nstdout preamble" as GITCTX <<app>>
    component "SmokeReady\nprints sentinel, sleeps" as SMOKE <<async>>
  }

  component "agent CLI\n(inherits the SHELL's env + cwd)" as AGENT <<app>>
}

SH ARROW_MAIN SHELLPRE : sourced lib, same process
SH ARROW_MAIN PREP : " ""proveo-entrypoint prep <target> || true"" "
PREP ARROW_MAIN OK : effects outlive the child
SHELLPRE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : cwd + exports inherited
SH ARROW_MAIN AGENT : " ""exec <agent> \"$@\""" "

note right of SHELLPRE
  **A child cannot mutate its parent.**
  ""chdir"" and ""setenv"" are per-process, so every
  step that sets them runs IN the shell the agent
  inherits. HISTORY: prep ran them too, exited 0, and
  the effects died with it — silently.
end note

note bottom of SH
  **Contract for def entrypoints.** Source the lib,
  run the prelude (""set_working_directory <dir>"",
  ""bridge_google_keys"", ""bridge_git_identity"") and the
  harness's own model bridge, THEN call ""prep"". Each
  fills only unset slots, so ""sbx run -e"" or
  ""--env-file"" values win. No step loads a workspace
  "".env"" (N7). See _spec/packages/lib/steps.puml.
end note

note top of SMOKE
  **Still owned by prep:** under ""PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST=1""
  ""prep"" prints ""PROVEO_SMOKE_READY"" and sleeps, so
  anything a def prints *after* ""prep"" is unreachable in
  smoke mode. Defs whose tests assert their own preamble
  must run ""prep"" with the flag cleared and call
  ""run_smoke_test"" at the end of their own preamble.
end note

note bottom of PREP
  **prep is the shared Go half, and only the half that can be.**
  Runtime user, git-context report, smoke mode — effects that live outside
  the process. HISTORY: it also bridged the Google keys, applied env
  bridges, bridged git identity and chdir'd (deleted with N1, 2026-10-17),
  loaded the workspace "".env"" (deleted with N7) and wrote the credential
  sentinel (deleted with D1, 2026-10-16).

  **Non-secret preferences travel by value** — the model and UI preferences
  from the shared baseline plus the harness's own ""config:"" list, as Kit
  environment. Secrets are declared in ""env:"" and travel through sbx's
  secret store instead.
end note

@enduml
